\viewkind4\uc1\pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. \cf0  Jesus, a good friend of my soul,
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0\qj A great love that you have for me
\par That makes you die on that great cross
\par Redeem and save us from our sins.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2.   My sins that have destroyed my life
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0  Hath brought a shame unto myself
\par  But thou hath laid me a table,
\par When I draw near I'm not sent out.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par  3.  I know that I am so unclean.
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0\qj A poor sinner and a pauper
\par I'm sick, condemned; and gone so blind.
\par Unjust, and I have gone naked
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par  4.  And you, our Lord our physician
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0\qj Our light that alway shine for us
\par Thou art the Master of all things.
\par Our good clothes are your righteousness
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5.  And so, Jesus I plead to you
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0 That come, heal me of my sickness
\par When I am dirty, cleanse me Lord
\par By thine own I shall then be clean.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\qj\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 6\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 6.  Through your own grace take my whole heart
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0  And put on the light of my faith;
\par \pard\li270\sl190\slmult0 When I am poor, make me so rich
\par That earthy things, be valueless.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li270\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 7\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 7.   Take from my heart all tastes away
\par \pard\li270\sl190\slmult0 And fill me with your love and faith.
\par Come in and stay in me O Lord
\par And let me join with you always
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li270\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 8\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 8.  Help me, and take my sins away
\par \pard\li270\sl190\slmult0  From me O Lord, on this table
\par And all the good thoughts in my head
\par Be strengthened by your spirit, Lord
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li270\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 9\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 9.   Come, drive away all enemies
\par \pard\li270\sl190\slmult0 Be King always in my poor heart,
\par And all the good thoughts in my head
\par Be strengthened by your spirit, Lord
\par 
\par \pard\fi-270\li270\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 10\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 10. Let all my life and my movement
\par \pard\li270\sl190\slmult0 Be so acceptable to thee
\par Advice me then that all my life
\par Shall be so well with you always
\par 
\par \pard\fi-270\li270\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 11\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 11. Before you, Jesus, shall come down
\par \pard\li270\sl190\slmult0 To take me from this earth, O Lord
\par To stay with you always in heav'n
\par \pard     That I shall be so satisfied!\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\f2\fs14 
\par }

